// #when C ... #else ... #end: the rules after #else run when C did not hold,
// and the two halves never both run in a cycle -- every cycle counts once,
// in Hi or in Lo. The condition is evaluated ONCE: the then-part jumps past
// the else-part. Nested, an inner #when's #else is the inner block's own.
#variable A = 0
#variable Hi = 0
#variable Lo = 0
#variable Even = 0
#variable Odd = 0
#variable Both = 0
A = A + 1
#when A > 3
  Hi = Hi + 1
  #when A % 2 == 0
    Even = Even + 1
  #else
    Odd = Odd + 1
  #end
#else
  Lo = Lo + 1
#end
Both = Hi + Lo
